{"number": 129, "text": "      Va        Whose         is this?        It’s  mine/yours/hers,                 etc.\n                             ‘\n\n       59                   I\n\n                   ( mine }      ( ours }   |   ( yours }  |   ( his )   |    (hers)         ( theirs )      |\n\n\n                                                                                        A |     ai      <=\n                       |       my           mine     ‘It’s my money.     It's mine.\n                    we    —    our          ours       It's our money.   It’s ours.\n                    you   —    your         yours      It's your money.  It's yours.\n                     he   —    his    — _   his        It's his money.   It's his.\n                    she        her    —_    hers       It’s her money.   It’s hers.\n                   they   —    their  —  __ theirs        their money. __ It’s theirs.\n\n        8       We  use my/your, etc, + noun (my hands / your book, etc.):\n                     ©  My  hands are cold.\n                     ©)  Is this your book?\n                     ©.  Emily gave me her umbrella.\n                     ©)  It’s their problem, not our problem.\n                 We use mine/yours, etc, without a noun:\n                     ©)       book  mine or yours? (= my book or your book)\n                      )         have an umbrella, so Emily gave me hers. (= her umbrella)\n                         It's their problem, not ours. (= not our problem)\n                     ©)  We went  in our car, and they went in theirs. (= their car)\n                 You can use his with or without a noun:\n                         “ls this his camera or hers?” “It's his.”\n                     ©)        to the movies with A friend of mine. (not A friend of me)\n                 A friend of mine / A friend of his / some friends of yours, etc.\n\n                     ©)  Tom  was in the restaurant with a friend of his. (not a friend of him)\n                     ©   Are those people friends of yours? (not friends of you)\n                                                                                                     Whose phone\n                         Whasee  phone is this? (= Is it vour phone? his phone? my phone?, etc.)        is this?\n                                                                                                        )\n                 You can use whose with or without a noun:\n\n                          Whose  money  is this?\n                         Whose   is this?\n                         Whose   shoes are these? |             ;\n                         Whose   are these?\n\n\n                 |             ELC.                                                                    7", "char_count": 2714, "mean_conf": 75.47, "word_count": 361, "words": [{"text": "|", "x0": 485, "y0": 880, "x1": 491, "y1": 915, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"text": "—>", "x0": 556, "y0": 883, "x1": 604, "y1": 912, "conf": 38, "bold": false}, {"text": "my", "x0": 667, "y0": 886, "x1": 729, "y1": 921, "conf": 92, "bold": false}, {"text": "—~", "x0": 819, "y0": 880, "x1": 868, "y1": 908, "conf": 6, "bold": false}, {"text": "mine", "x0": 942, "y0": 872, "x1": 1045, "y1": 909, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "‘It’s", "x0": 1150, "y0": 842, "x1": 1231, "y1": 921, "conf": 45, "bold": false}, {"text": "my", "x0": 1245, "y0": 879, "x1": 1307, "y1": 914, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "money.", "x0": 1322, "y0": 877, "x1": 1461, "y1": 912, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "It's", "x0": 1576, "y0": 863, "x1": 1624, "y1": 901, "conf": 70, "bold": false}, {"text": "mine.", "x0": 1638, "y0": 863, "x1": 1750, "y1": 900, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "we", "x0": 439, "y0": 950, "x1": 493, "y1": 976, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"text": "—", "x0": 557, "y0": 944, "x1": 605, "y1": 971, "conf": 74, "bold": false}, {"text": "our", "x0": 666, "y0": 946, "x1": 739, "y1": 973, "conf": 92, "bold":